# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Code Integration
Modified `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component in the body section, placed after the existing `<Analytics />` component

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the Next.js App Router (v13.5+) pattern as specified in the official Vercel documentation:
- Used the `/next` import path for Next.js-specific integration
- Placed the component in the root layout file for site-wide tracking
- Positioned alongside the existing Vercel Analytics component for consistency

## Verification

✅ **Build Test**: Successfully completed `npm run build` with no errors
✅ **Linting**: Ran `npm run lint` - no new errors introduced by our changes
✅ **Type Checking**: TypeScript compilation successful (no type errors)
✅ **Lock Files**: Updated package-lock.json appropriately

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics
2. Data will become available in the Vercel dashboard after several days of visitor activity
3. Access metrics via Project → Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard

## Notes

- The project already had `@vercel/analytics` installed, so this addition complements the existing analytics setup
- Speed Insights provides Core Web Vitals and performance metrics
- No additional configuration required - the component works out of the box on Vercel deployments
